<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trinh Bong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1740">1740</a>–<a href="/years/1787">1787</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Trịnh Bồng</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trinh Bong was the last of the Trinh lords who ruled northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in the name of the Le emperors. He was installed in 1786 after the Tay Son had overthrown <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinh-khai">Trinh Khai</a>, but the Le emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-chieu-thong">Le Chieu Thong</a> and his ally Nguyen Huu Chinh opposed him, and he fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thang Long</a> in 1787, ending more than two centuries of Trinh rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trinh-bong.jpg" alt="Trinh Bong" width="113" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Trịnh Như Tấu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tr%E1%BB%8Bnh_B%E1%BB%93ng.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
